diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0dc0653
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+Feature: localStorage persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to survive page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Save on create
+
+  Scenario: Created todos are persisted to localStorage
+    Given localStorage is empty
+    When I create a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage contains a todo with id and title "Buy milk" and completed false
+
+  Scenario: Empty localStorage loads an empty todo list
+    Given localStorage is empty
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Rule: Save on toggle
+
+  Scenario: Completed state is persisted after reload
+    Given localStorage is empty
+    When I create a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    And I toggle "Buy milk" as completed
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" has class "completed"
+
+  Rule: Save on edit
+
+  Scenario: Edited title is persisted after reload
+    Given localStorage is empty
+    When I create a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    And I edit the todo "Buy milk" to "Buy oat milk"
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Rule: Save on delete
+
+  Scenario: Deleted todos are removed from localStorage
+    Given localStorage is empty
+    When I create a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    And I destroy the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Rule: Persisted filter state
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is restored on reload
+    Given localStorage is empty
+    When I create a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    And I create a todo titled "Second"
+    And I toggle "Buy milk" as completed
+    And I navigate to "#/active"
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo list shows only active todos
+    And the active count is correct
