@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+Feature: Hash routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by active/completed status
+  So that I can focus on what remains or review what is done
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+    And localStorage is empty
+    And 2 active todos and 1 completed todo exist
+
+  Rule: Default route — all
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    When the app renders
+    Then the todo list shows 3 items
+    And the "All" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Rule: Active route
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Rule: Completed route
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    When I navigate to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the "Completed" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Rule: Filter persistence
+
+  Scenario: Filter persists when toggling completion
+    Given I am viewing active todos
+    When I toggle the first visible todo as completed
+    Then that todo is removed from the visible list
+    And the active count updates
+
+  Rule: #/! allowed alternative
+
+  Scenario: Navigating to "#/" shows all
+    Given I am viewing "#/active"
+    When I navigate to "#/"
+    Then the todo list shows 3 items
+
+  Scenario: Items updated in filtered view are shown or hidden accordingly
+    Given I am viewing active todos
+    When I toggle the first visible todo as completed
+    Then that todo is hidden from the active list
+    And when I navigate to "#/completed"
+    Then that todo appears in the completed list
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todos.feature b/features/todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..14ef9c1
